%I A398683 #32 Aug 29 2026 12:31:33
%S A398683 25,29,43,79,135,534,1477
%N A398683 Numbers k such that C(k,5) = C(x,5) + C(y,5) + C(z,5) is solvable, where k > x >= y >= z > 5.
%C A398683 135 has two solutions, since C(78,5) + C(133,5) = C(117,5) + C(118,5).
%C A398683 a(8), if it exists, exceeds 2*10^4.
%C A398683 Assuming that (a, b, c, d) is an integer solution to C(k,5) = C(x,5) + C(y,5) + C(z,5), where k > x >= y >= z > 5, a computer search shows that any new solution would have to satisfy k - z > 500.
%e A398683 C(25,5) = C(22,5) + C(22,5) + C(11,5).
%e A398683 C(29,5) = C(28,5) + C(21,5) + C(9,5).
%e A398683 C(43,5) = C(40,5) + C(34,5) + C(22,5).
%e A398683 C(79,5) = C(78,5) + C(42,5) + C(39,5).
%e A398683 C(135,5) = C(133,5) + C(78,5) + C(57,5).
%e A398683 C(135,5) = C(118,5) + C(117,5) + C(57,5).
%e A398683 C(534,5) = C(531,5) + C(262,5) + C(19,5).
%e A398683 C(1477,5) = C(1315,5) + C(1230,5) + C(781,5).
